# artifacts/agent_runtime/ was ignored wholesale until 2026-08-23. That rule destroyed an entire
# experimental arm: the Anthropic caches and budget ledger were never committed, lived only on one
# machine's ephemeral disk, and vanished with it (docs/PROVIDER_HANDOFF_STATE.md).
#
# The tree is NOT blanket-safe to commit. What is committable is narrow and deliberate:
# interpretations of SYNTHETIC BENCHMARK inputs, which are generated from a seeded corpus, contain
# no real person's data, and are paid, slow and irreproducible once a moving model alias moves.
# Those are primary evidence and belong in version control.
#
# What must NEVER be committed: real user inputs, production data, credentials, or model
# interpretations derived from any real person. `tests/runtime-cache-policy.test.ts` enforces this
# rather than trusting the comment, and the two ignore rules below are the default-deny for the
# paths where non-synthetic material would land.
artifacts/agent_runtime/**/user/
artifacts/agent_runtime/**/production/
